WEBVTT

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.800
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.900
Sammy.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.000
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.700
Now Dean, go!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.300
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.900
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.300
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.100
I can't do this alone.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.700
No! Jess!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.200
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.700
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.400
Be advised. We've found the victim.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.300
She's alive.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.300
It's okay. It's okay.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.600
In there.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.500
Let's go.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.100
Freeze!

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.100
Don't move! Drop the knife!

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.700
Keep your hands where
I can see them! Drop it.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.200
Hold it right there! Come on, come on!

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.300
Now!

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.300
Nice and easy!

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.500
Do it!

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.000
Alright, I figure we hit
Tucancary by lunch then head South.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.100
And best be by midnight.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.500
Sam wears women's underwear...

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.900
I've been listening, I'm just busy.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.400
Busy doing what?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.100
Reading e-Mails.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.800
E-Mails from who? From
my friends at Stanford.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.100
You kidding? You still keep in
touch with your college buddies?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.800
Why not?

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.800
Well...

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.300
What do you exactly tell them?

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.800
You know, about...

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.400
Where you've been
What you've been doing.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.600
I tell them I'm on a road
trip with my big brother.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.600
I tell them I need some
time off after Jess.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.100
Oh, I see you lie to them?

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.400
No.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.200
I just don't tell them everything.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.800
Yeah, dude. That's called lying.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.200
I mean, hey man. I get it. Telling
them the truth is far worse.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.600
So what am I suppose to do? Just
cut everybody out of my life?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.800
You're serious? Look, it sucks but...

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.500
In a job like this you can't
get close to people, period.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.900
You're kind of
anti-Social, you know that?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.000
You know, whatever.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.200
God. What?

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.000
This e-Mail from Rebecca Warren
one of those friends of mine.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.600
Is she hot?

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.400
I went to school with
her and her brother Zach.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.900
She says, Zach's been
charged with murder.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.500
He's been arrested for
killing his girlfriend.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.800
Rebecca says he didn't do it but...

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.600
Sounds like the cops
have a pretty good case.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.100
Dude, what kind of people
are you hanging out with?

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.200
No man, I know Zach. He's no killer.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.300
Then maybe you know Zach
as well as he knows you.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.400
St. Louis, we're going.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.400
I'm sorry about you buddy, okay?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.500
But this doesn't sound
like our kind of problem.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.100
It is our problem. They're my friends.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.500
St. Louis is 400 miles behind us, Sam.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.300
Oh, my god! Sam! Well
if it isn't little Becky?

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.000
You know you could do
that little Becky crap.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.800
I got your e-Mail. I didn't
think you would come here.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.600
Dean, older brother.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.300
Hi. Hi.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.700
We're here to help.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.400
Whatever we can do.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.800
Come in.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.300
Nice place. It's my parents.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.600
I was just crashing here for the
long weekend when everything happened.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:15.400
I decided to take this semester off.
I'm gonna stay until Zach's free.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.600
Where are your folks?

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.300
They live in Paris for half the year

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.100
So they're on their way
home now for the trial.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.100
Do you guys want a beer
or something? / Yeah...

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.500
No, thanks.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.700
So, tell us what happened.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.600
Well...

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.400
Zach came home and he
found Emily tied to a chair.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.500
And she was beaten up and bloody
and she wasn't breathing and so he

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.500
He called 911 and the
police they showed up and..

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.600
And they arrested him.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.900
But the thing is the only way that Zach

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:52.600
Could have killed Emily if he was
in two places at the same time.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.300
The police they have a video.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.300
It's from the security
tape from across the street.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:02.100
And it shows Zach coming home at 10:30.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.400
Now, Emily was killed just after that

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.900
But I swear he was here with me

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.800
Having a few beers until
at least after midnight.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.000
You know, maybe we could see
the crime scene. Zach's house...

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.800
We could.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.500
Why? I mean what could you do?

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.100
Me? Not much but Dean's a cop.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.400
A detective actually.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.700
Really? Where?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.900
Bisbee Arizona.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.200
But I'm off duty now.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:40.200
You guys are so nice to
offer but I don't know...

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.100
Beck, I know Zach didn't do this.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.100
Now, we have to find a way
to prove that he's innocent.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.900
Okay.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.500
I'm gonna go get the keys.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.700
Oh, yeah man. You're a real
straight shooter with your friends.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.000
Look...

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.200
Zach and Becky need our help.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.900
I just don't think this
is our kind of problem.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.400
Two places at once?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.100
We've looked into less.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.600
You're sure this is okay?

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:36.100
Yeah, I am an officer of the law.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.700
Beck, you want to wait outside?

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:59.000
No, I wanna help.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.100
Tell us what else the police said.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.600
Well...

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.900
There's no sign of a break in.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.300
They said Emily let her attacker in.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.300
And the lawyers, they're already
talking about plead bargain.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.500
Oh, god.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.700
Look, Beck.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.800
If Zach didn't do this

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.600
It means somebody else did.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.600
And idea who?

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.000
There was something.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.100
About a week before
somebody broke in here

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.400
And stole some clothes.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:47.700
Zach's clothes. And the police
they don't think it's anything.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.100
We were not that far from downtown.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:53.900
Sometimes people get robbed.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.300
You know, that used
to be the sweetest dog.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.500
What happened?

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.900
He just changed. You
remember when he changed?

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.600
I guess around the time of the murder.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.100
Listen, the neighbor's dog went psycho

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.400
Right around the time
Zach's girlfriend was killed.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.000
And most ??? Has a shock
since the paranormal.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.700
Yeah, maybe Fighto saw something.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.300
So, you think this is
our kind of problem?

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.100
No, probably not.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.500
But we should look at the
security tape just to make sure.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.400
Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.200
So, the tape. The security footage.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.600
You think maybe your lawyers
can get their hands on it.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.600
I just don't have that
kind of a jurisdiction..

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:51.900
I've already got it.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.800
I don't want to say
something in front of the cop.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.000
I stole it off the lawyer's desk.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.500
I just had to see it for myself.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.400
Alright.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.600
I'll miss you.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.800
Why do they always have to send you?

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.200
Because I'm the best.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.200
I know, that's why I
want you to stay home.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.700
It's just Kansas City.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.500
I'll be home tomorrow night

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.200
And make it up to you.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.400
You better.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.400
Here he comes.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.700
22:04, that's just after 10.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.400
You said the time of
death is about 10:30.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.200
Our lawyers hired some
kind of video expert.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.400
He says the tapes are authentic.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.000
It wasn't tampered with.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.700
Hey, Beck.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.400
Can we take those beers now?

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.000
Oh, sure.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.800
Hey...

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:35.700
Maybe some sandwiches too?

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.400
What do you think this, Hooters?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.300
I wish.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.800
What is it? Check this out.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.900
Maybe it's just a camera flare.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.300
That's not like any camera
flare I've ever seen.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.400
You know a lot of cultures believed

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.700
That a photograph can catch
a glimpse of the soul. Right.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.100
You remember the dog
that was freaking out?

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.400
Maybe he saw this thing.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.000
Maybe this is some kind
of dark double of Zach.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.400
It's something that looks
like him but isn't him.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.900
Like a Doppelganger? Yeah.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:10.100
That sure explains how he
was in two places at once.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.200
Honey, it's me.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:26.100
The client canceled at the last minute.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.800
I called, why didn't you answer?

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.700
Lindsey?

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.700
Lindsey?

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:45.400
Lindsey?

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.900
It's okay Lindsey. It's me.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.900
Please, don't hurt me anymore.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.900
Leave me alone.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:59.900
Alright. What are we doing
here at 5:30 in the morning?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.400
I realized something.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.800
The video tape shows the killer
going in but not coming out.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.700
So he came out the back door?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.200
Right. So there should
be a trail to follow.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.700
A trail the police will never pursue.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.400
Cause they think the killer never left
they caught your friend Zach inside.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:18.900
Still don't know what we're
doing here at 5:30 in the morning.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.200
Blood.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.100
Somebody came this way.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.700
Maybe the trail ends I
don't see anything over here.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.100
What happened?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:59.900
He tried to kill his wife.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.600
Tied her up and beat her.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:02.800
Really?

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:07.200
I used to see him go to work in the
morning. He'd wave and say hello.

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:09.800
He seemed like such a nice guy.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:36.000
Hey.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.500
Remember I said this isn't
our kind of problem? Yeah.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.600
It's definitely our kind of
problem. What did you find out?

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.500
I just talked to the patrolmen
who was first in the scene.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.100
I heard this guy Alex's story.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.600
Apparently what he did was driving home

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:47.500
From a business trip
when he was attacked.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.600
So he was at two
places at once. Exactly.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.700
Then he sees himself in the
house, police says he's a nut job.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:58.000
Two dark doubles attacking loved
ones in exactly the same way.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.600
Could be the same thing doing it too.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.800
Shape Shifter?

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.500
Something that can make
itself look like anyone?

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:07.100
Every culture in the world
has a Shape Shifter lure.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:10.300
The legends of creatures who can
transform itself into animals or other men.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.000
Right, skinwalkers, werewolves...

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.900
We got two attacks from
them blocks from each other.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:17.400
I'm guessing we got a Shape
Shifter problem in the neighborhood.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:20.500
Let me ask you this. And
all this Shape Shifter lure.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.100
Can any of them fly?

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.000
Not that I know of. I
picked up a trail here.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.100
Someone ran out of back of this
building, headed off this way.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.800
Just like you're friend's house. Yeah.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:35.500
And just like in Zach's
house the trail suddenly ends.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.500
Whatever it is It just...

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.800
Disappeared.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.500
Well, there's another way to go.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.000
Down.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.700
I bet this runs right
by Zach's house too.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:11.200
The Shape Shifter can be using
the sewer system to get around.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.100
I think you're right.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.600
Look at this.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:25.300
Is this from his victims?

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.300
You know I just had a sick thought.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.300
When the Shape Shifter changes shape...

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.900
Maybe it sheds.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.800
That is sick.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.900
One thing I learned from dad.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.300
No matter what kind
of Shape Shifter it is.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:48.500
There's one sure way to kill it.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.600
Silver bullet to the
heart. That's right.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.100
This is Sam. Where are you?

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.300
We're near Zach's. We're
just checking some things out.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:01.400
Well look Sam, just stop cause I
really don't need your help anymore.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:02.700
What are you talking about?

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:05.600
I told the lawyers we
went to the crime scene.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:06.900
Why would you do that?

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.800
I told them that we're
with a police officer

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:12.800
And they checked it out and they told me
that there is no detective Dean Winchester.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:16.800
Beck... I don't understand why you would
lie to me about something like that.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.200
We're trying to help.
Oh, trying to help.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.600
Do you realize that that
was a sealed crime scene.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.100
This could have just ruined Zach's case.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.000
Beck, I'm sorry...

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.800
No, goodbye Sam.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.600
I hate to say it but that's
exactly what I'm talking about.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.600
You lie to your friends because if they
know the real you they'd be freaked.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.200
It's just...

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.900
It'll be easier... If I was like you.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:54.300
Hey, man. Like it or not.
We are not like other people.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:58.000
But I'll tell you one
thing. This whole gig.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.900
It ain't without purpose.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.800
I think we're close to its lair.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.900
Why do you say that?

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.800
Cause there's another puking
dousing vile next to your face.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.300
Oh, god.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.000
Looks like he's lived here for a while.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.000
Who knows how many
murders he's got away with.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.100
Dean!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.200
Get the son of a bitch.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:53.800
Alright, let's split up.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.500
Alright, I'll meet you
around the inside. Alright.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:34.900
Hey.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:38.800
Anything?

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.300
No, he's gone.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.300
Alright, let's get back to the car.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:00.600
You think he found
another way underground?

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:02.000
Yeah, probably.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.800
You got the keys?

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:11.900
Hey, didn't dad once face a
Shape Shifter in San Antonio?

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:13.300
That was Auston.

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:16.600
It didn't turn out to be a Shape
Shifter it was a Thought Form.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.500
A psychic projection, remember?

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:21.900
Alright.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.400
Here you go.

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:41.900
Don't move!

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.500
What have you done with him?

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:44.900
Dude, chill.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:46.900
It's me, alright? No, I don't think so.

00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:49.500
Where's my brother?
You're about to shoot him.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:52.000
Sam, calm down. You got
those keys with your left.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:53.300
Your shoulder was hurt.

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:54.300
Yeah, it's better.

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:55.500
What do you want me to do? Cry?

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:57.500
You're not my brother.

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.000
Won't you pull the trigger then?

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.600
Cause you're not sure.

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:04.200
Dude, you know me.

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:05.700
Don't.

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:42.200
Where is he?

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:44.700
Where's Dean?

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:48.500
I wouldn't worry about him.

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:50.500
I would worry about you.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:52.200
Where is he?

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:55.600
You don't really want to know.

00:23:57.700 --> 00:24:01.600
I swear the more I learn
about you and your family...

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:04.700
I thought I came from a bad background.

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:07.300
What do you mean learn?

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:31.000
He sure got issues with you.

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:33.600
You got to go to college.

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:35.700
He had to stay home.

00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:39.700
I mean, I had to stay home. With dad.

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:41.600
You don't think I had dreams of my own?

00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:43.600
But dad needed me.

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:46.700
Where the hell were
you? Where is my brother?

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:49.300
I'm your brother.

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.600
You see, deep down...

00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:55.000
I'm just jealous.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.800
You got friends you can have a life.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:02.800
Me? I know I'm a freak.

00:25:02.800 --> 00:25:06.000
And sooner or later
everybody's gonna leave me.

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:09.000
What are you talking about?

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
You left.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Hell, I did everything dad asked
me to and he ditched me too.

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:17.100
No explanation, nothing. Just poof.

00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:22.200
Left me with your sorry ass.

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:28.700
But still this life

00:25:28.700 --> 00:25:31.100
It's not without it's perch.

00:25:31.400 --> 00:25:34.600
I met the nicest people.

00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:36.800
Like little Becky.

00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:40.200
You know Dean would bang
her if he had the chance.

00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:43.000
Let's see what happens.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:55.700
Oh, hi.

00:25:55.700 --> 00:25:57.500
I know what you're
gonna say. Oh, you do.

00:25:57.500 --> 00:25:59.000
Well no, not exactly.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.000
But I could take a guess.

00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:03.300
Get off my porch.

00:26:03.900 --> 00:26:05.700
That's about right.

00:26:06.100 --> 00:26:10.100
I admit we lied thought
I tried to explain myself.

00:26:10.100 --> 00:26:11.700
Sam told me not to come but

00:26:11.700 --> 00:26:14.700
I thought what the hell I have to try.

00:26:20.700 --> 00:26:22.100
Damn it!

00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:29.700
That better be you Sam and
not that freaking nature.

00:26:30.100 --> 00:26:31.600
Yeah, it's me.

00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:34.700
He went to Becky's looking like you.

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:36.800
Well, he's not stupid.

00:26:37.500 --> 00:26:39.700
He picked the handsome one.

00:26:44.800 --> 00:26:46.200
So, you're saying that

00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:51.000
There's something out there that
made itself look like my brother?

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:54.500
What did you call it? The Shape Shifter.

00:26:55.400 --> 00:26:58.400
Yeah, maybe we're crazy.

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:00.500
But what if we're not?

00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:03.800
I mean look, you said it yourself.
That Zach was in two places at once.

00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:07.200
Tell me how that can happen?
Okay, so... this thing.

00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:10.600
It can make itself look like anybody?

00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:12.100
That's right.

00:27:12.300 --> 00:27:13.700
What is it? Like a...

00:27:13.700 --> 00:27:15.900
Genetic freak?

00:27:17.600 --> 00:27:19.400
Maybe.

00:27:21.200 --> 00:27:23.500
Evolution is about mutation.

00:27:23.500 --> 00:27:25.400
Right?

00:27:25.400 --> 00:27:29.000
So, maybe this thing was born human

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:31.400
But was different.

00:27:31.600 --> 00:27:35.000
Hideous and hated.

00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:39.200
Until he learned to become someone else.

00:27:43.400 --> 00:27:45.000
Yeah, that's the thing.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.700
He didn't just look like you he was you.

00:27:47.700 --> 00:27:50.300
Or at least becoming
you. What do you mean?

00:27:50.300 --> 00:27:54.300
I don't know, it was like he was
downloading your thoughts and memories.

00:27:54.400 --> 00:27:56.300
You mean, like the Volking Mindmill?

00:27:56.300 --> 00:27:57.800
Yeah, something like that.

00:27:57.800 --> 00:28:00.700
I mean, maybe that's why
it didn't just kill us.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.300
Maybe he needs to keep us alive.

00:28:07.600 --> 00:28:08.800
Psychic connection?

00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:10.000
Hands.

00:28:10.400 --> 00:28:11.400
Yeah.

00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:14.300
Go. We've got to go. He's
probably at Rebecca's already.

00:28:16.100 --> 00:28:19.100
Come on. We got to find
a phone call the police.

00:28:19.100 --> 00:28:22.800
Whoa, whoa, whoa. You're
gonna put an APB on me?

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:24.400
Sorry.

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:26.200
This way.

00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:33.100
It's funny.

00:28:33.900 --> 00:28:35.600
I kind of understand him.

00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:37.800
He's all alone.

00:28:38.600 --> 00:28:40.700
Close to no one.

00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:43.600
All he wants is for someone to love him.

00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:48.700
He's like me.

00:28:53.300 --> 00:28:55.500
Everybody needs...

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:59.300
A little human touch now and then.

00:28:59.500 --> 00:29:01.400
It's so hard to be different.

00:29:01.400 --> 00:29:03.100
You should go.

00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:13.500
You are disgusting! Just
get the hell out of here!

00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:15.700
Rebecca, just calm down. I'll calm down!

00:29:15.700 --> 00:29:18.500
What is wrong with you?
What's wrong with me?

00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:19.700
What's wrong with you?

00:29:19.700 --> 00:29:21.600
I'm calling the police.

00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:36.700
Give me your hands!

00:29:37.500 --> 00:29:38.700
Shut up!

00:29:43.300 --> 00:29:45.700
You're a nice girl, Rebecca.

00:29:46.300 --> 00:29:48.100
I mean, I liked you.

00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:53.000
Believe me, it makes this harder.

00:29:56.100 --> 00:29:58.900
But I got to do what I got to do.

00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:41.900
Freeze!

00:30:42.100 --> 00:30:43.300
Call off the knife.

00:30:43.300 --> 00:30:44.700
Drop the knife!

00:30:44.900 --> 00:30:46.600
Drop the knife!

00:30:50.200 --> 00:30:51.400
Come on, come on.

00:30:51.900 --> 00:30:52.600
Go, go!

00:32:03.700 --> 00:32:06.900
An anonymous tip led police to
a home in the central west end

00:32:06.900 --> 00:32:10.400
Where a squad team discovered
a local woman found engaged.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:14.300
Her attacker a white male
approximately 24 to 30 years of age

00:32:14.300 --> 00:32:16.500
Was discovered hiding in the home.

00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:18.400
Shots were fired... Man!

00:32:18.600 --> 00:32:20.100
It's not even a good picture.

00:32:20.100 --> 00:32:21.600
It's good enough.

00:32:23.700 --> 00:32:24.900
Man.

00:32:29.200 --> 00:32:31.100
God. Come on!

00:32:33.700 --> 00:32:35.400
At least attempted
murder unless we know...

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:36.800
I didn't kill her!

00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:38.700
I'm gonna check Rebecca in the
morning. See if she's alright.

00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:40.500
Alright, first I want to
find that handsome devil

00:32:40.500 --> 00:32:42.100
And kick the holy crap out of him.

00:32:42.100 --> 00:32:43.800
We have no weapons. No silver bullets.

00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:45.500
Man, the guy's walking
around with my face, okay?

00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:48.000
It's a little personal,
I want to find him.

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:50.000
Okay.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.300
Where do we look? We can
start with the sewers.

00:32:52.300 --> 00:32:53.800
We have no weapons.

00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:56.400
He stole our guns. We need more.

00:32:58.400 --> 00:32:59.500
The car?

00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.900
I'm betting he drove
them over to Rebecca's.

00:33:00.900 --> 00:33:04.400
The news said he was on foot.
I bet it's still parked there.

00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:06.400
The thought of him driving my car!

00:33:06.400 --> 00:33:07.700
Oh, come on.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.000
But it's killing me! Let it go.

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:22.700
There she is.

00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:26.000
Finally something right tonight.

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:30.300
Oh, crap.

00:33:36.500 --> 00:33:37.800
This way, this way!

00:33:38.100 --> 00:33:39.100
You go, I'll hold them off.

00:33:39.100 --> 00:33:40.400
What are you talking
about? They'll catch you.

00:33:40.400 --> 00:33:41.500
Look, they can't hold me!

00:33:41.500 --> 00:33:44.600
Just go! Keep out of
sight! Meet me at Rebecca's.

00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:47.700
Dean! Stay out of the sewers alone!

00:33:48.100 --> 00:33:49.700
I mean it! Yeah, yeah!

00:33:49.700 --> 00:33:50.900
Don't move.

00:33:50.900 --> 00:33:53.400
Keep your hands where I can see them.

00:34:01.600 --> 00:34:03.300
I'm sorry Sam.

00:34:03.300 --> 00:34:05.100
You know me.

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:06.900
I just can't wait.

00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:45.200
Rebecca?

00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:47.800
So, say the Shape Shifter is real.

00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:50.100
By the way you know you're crazy?

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:53.400
But um.. Say it is real.

00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:55.600
How do you stop it?

00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:57.100
Thanks.

00:34:57.600 --> 00:34:59.800
Silver bullet to the heart.

00:35:00.800 --> 00:35:02.500
You are crazy.

00:35:05.700 --> 00:35:07.300
What happened?

00:35:07.500 --> 00:35:10.700
I was walking home and
everything just went white.

00:35:10.700 --> 00:35:11.600
Somebody hit me over the head

00:35:11.600 --> 00:35:15.500
And I rounded up just in time
to see that thing turn into me.

00:35:15.500 --> 00:35:17.900
How is that even possible? Okay, okay.

00:35:17.900 --> 00:35:18.900
It's okay.

00:35:18.900 --> 00:35:20.800
Come on. Can you walk?

00:35:20.800 --> 00:35:22.000
Okay, we've got to hurry.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:23.800
Sam went to see you.

00:35:32.400 --> 00:35:34.400
What are you gonna do to me?

00:35:34.700 --> 00:35:36.700
I'm not gonna do anything.

00:35:36.700 --> 00:35:38.600
Dean will though.

00:35:40.300 --> 00:35:41.700
You'll never catch him.

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:43.900
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:35:44.600 --> 00:35:47.500
Murder on the first his own brother.

00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:50.100
He'll be hunted the rest of his life.

00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:57.500
I must say,

00:35:57.500 --> 00:36:00.000
I will be sorry to lose this skin.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.000
Your brother's got a
lot of good qualities.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:06.100
You should appreciate more than you do.

00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:08.500
Cheers.

00:36:36.200 --> 00:36:37.800
You son of a bitch!

00:36:46.100 --> 00:36:47.500
Not bad, little brother.

00:36:47.500 --> 00:36:49.100
You're not him.

00:37:04.400 --> 00:37:06.300
Even when we were kids

00:37:06.300 --> 00:37:08.600
I always kicked your ass.

00:37:43.700 --> 00:37:45.000
Hey!

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:10.400
Sam!

00:38:46.300 --> 00:38:47.900
So, this is what you do?

00:38:47.900 --> 00:38:51.700
You and your brother you hunt
down these kind of things.

00:38:51.700 --> 00:38:53.800
Yeah, pretty much. I can't believe it!

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:57.000
I mean I saw with my own eyes and...

00:38:57.200 --> 00:38:58.900
Does everybody at school...

00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:01.200
Nobody knows that you do this?

00:39:01.200 --> 00:39:02.500
No.

00:39:02.800 --> 00:39:05.000
Did Jessica know?

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.200
No, she didn't.

00:39:09.800 --> 00:39:11.600
Must be lonely.

00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:13.900
Oh, no. No, it's not that bad.

00:39:13.900 --> 00:39:17.100
Anyway what can I do? It's my family.

00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:20.100
Well you know Zach and me
and everybody at school.

00:39:20.100 --> 00:39:22.600
We really miss you.

00:39:23.500 --> 00:39:25.200
Yeah, me too.

00:39:28.400 --> 00:39:31.900
Well, will you call sometime?

00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:35.000
It might not be for a little while.

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:52.700
So what about your friend Zach?

00:39:52.700 --> 00:39:57.400
Cops are blaming this Dean
Winchester guy for Emily's murder.

00:39:57.400 --> 00:39:59.700
They found the weapon in the guy's lair,

00:39:59.700 --> 00:40:02.300
Zach's clothes stained with her blood.

00:40:02.300 --> 00:40:05.700
Now they're thinking maybe the
surveillance tapes were tampered with.

00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:09.100
Yeah, Beck says Zach
would be released soon.

00:40:19.300 --> 00:40:20.800
Sorry man.

00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:24.200
About what?

00:40:25.300 --> 00:40:27.000
I really wish things could
be different, you know.

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:29.000
I wish you could be

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.400
Joe College. Na, that's okay.

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:33.700
You know, the truth is...

00:40:33.700 --> 00:40:36.000
Even in Stanford deep
down I really never fit in.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:38.000
That's cause you're a freak.

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:39.000
Yeah, thanks.

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:40.900
I'm a freak too.

00:40:41.100 --> 00:40:43.500
I'm right there with you all the way.

00:40:44.500 --> 00:40:46.700
Yeah, I know you are.

00:40:47.800 --> 00:40:50.000
You know, I got to say.

00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:52.800
I'm sorry I'm gonna miss it. Miss what?

00:40:53.100 --> 00:40:56.400
How many chances am I gonna
have to see my own funeral?



